# MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Distributing station
#
# Umbrella of this use case: the ontology header, which imports the module files under core/ and ext/.
# Single-file form: distributing-merged.ttl (written by tools/merge_usecases.py).
#
# Notes carried over from the former plant.ttl, product.ttl, which this use case was split from;
# section titles and file names in them refer to those files.
#
# [plant.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - DISTRIBUTING STATION - PLANT (DESIGN TIME)
#
# Sources: 648811_Manual_Distributing (DE/EN 04/06 R2.2),
# 01_Distributing_
# GRAFCET.pdf (DE 01/04), Function.pdf, Function0.pdf and Changer.pdf in
# 'Distributing Station design documents'.
#
# The circuit diagrams and parts list of this station are only on the
# Festo CD-ROM 665871, which is not among the documents. So the signals
# below have no PLC address, terminal bit or BMK; they are named after
# the
# GRAFCET transitions and actions. Part numbers come from the manual's
# data-sheet list; quantities are not stated.
#
# STATION
#
# Station 1 of the MPS numbering. Order number 648811 is that of the
# manual; the station material number is not stated.
#
# TECHNICAL DATA
#
# Static values from the manual's technical-data table and commissioning
# section.
#
# BILL OF MATERIALS
#
# No parts list for this station is among the documents: the nodes are
# the data-sheet list of the manual, quantities not stated.
#
# SIGNALS (DATA POINTS)
#
# Direction is from the PLC's view in the 'dir' sense of the manual: a
# sensor
# signal is an maestro:Output of the station (maestro:DtdlTelemetry), an actuator
# command an maestro:Input (maestro:DtdlProperty). Ten station signals for the 7 +
# 7
# I/O of the technical data; how the commands map onto outputs is not
# stated.
#
# I/O PATH: SYSLINK ENDPOINTS AND DATA INTERFACES
#
# The URNs name the SysLink connectors; there is no network address in
# the documents.
#
# SKILLS
#
# One atomic skill per GRAFCET action; DistributeWorkpiece is the cycle.
#
# [product.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - DISTRIBUTING STATION - PRODUCT (RECIPES)
#
# Source: the GRAFCET function chart of the Distributing station
# (01_Distributing_GRAFCET.pdf).
#
# The station's control sequence as an maestro:Recipe. Steps are realised by
# the skills of plant.ttl; data bindings connect parameters declared
# there. The workpiece itself and the line recipe are in
# line/product.ttl.
#
# CONTROL SEQUENCE (GRAFCET)
#
# One maestro:PlanStep per GRAFCET step with an action; maestro:stepOrder is the
# GRAFCET step number. Empty steps (1 start, 5 cycle start, 7 'downstream
# station free', 9 magazine status) and the flag-only step 4 are folded
# into the transition expressions of the control-flow constraints.
# Alternative = OR-divergence, Loop = jump back.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Distributing station"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The Festo MPS Distributing station of the LTU line: modules, components, signals, skills, safety and care. The GRAFCET control sequence is an HHM-Core recipe in core/recipe.ttl. Built from the station manual 648811, its GRAFCET and the Function / Changer sheets."@en ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/invocation>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/maas>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/policy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/product>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/recipe>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/resource>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/core/skill>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/automationml>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/dtdl>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/energy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/isa95>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/maintenance>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/ext/runtime>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/shared> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .
